---
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
	title="Community"
	description="Community guidance for discussing Citizen Stewardship proposals in a serious, nonpartisan way."
>
	<PageHero
		title="Community Review"
		lede="Citizen Stewardship is strongest when people read carefully, argue honestly, and test reform ideas against practical limits."
	/>

	<section class="section tight">
		<div class="container two-grid">
			<article class="info-panel">
				<h2>Discussion ground rules</h2>
				<ul class="quiet-list">
					<li>Focus on rules and institutions, not party loyalty.</li>
					<li>Separate what is desirable from what is legally possible.</li>
					<li>Name tradeoffs, enforcement problems, and unintended consequences.</li>
					<li>Protect rights, minority viewpoints, and lawful dissent.</li>
					<li>Prefer plain language over slogans.</li>
				</ul>
			</article>
			<article class="info-panel">
				<h2>Local use</h2>
				<p>
					The proposals can support reading groups, classroom discussion, civic association
					meetings, local reform workshops, or issue-by-issue review sessions.
				</p>
				<p>
					A useful meeting format is simple: pick one section, summarize its goal, list the legal
					and political barriers, then write concrete revisions.
				</p>
			</article>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section surface-band">
		<div class="container content-grid">
			<div class="prose">
				<h2>Questions worth asking</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>What problem is this reform trying to solve?</li>
					<li>What power does it create, limit, or transfer?</li>
					<li>Who enforces it, and how could enforcement fail?</li>
					<li>What rights need explicit protection?</li>
					<li>Can a smaller pilot test the idea before national adoption?</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<aside class="callout">
				<h3>Next step</h3>
				<p>
					Use the submit page to prepare specific, source-aware feedback. This site does not run
					an online intake form.
				</p>
				<a class="button primary" href="/submit">Prepare feedback</a>
			</aside>
		</div>
	</section>
</SiteLayout>
